{"op":"add","key":"TRACE-2","patternType":"ubiquitous","systemName":"trace-consolidation phase","systemResponse":"write only candidate memories whose signal exceeds what one transcript grep surfaces","priority":"critical","status":"implemented","verificationMethod":"inspection","verificationNote":"SHIPPED. apps/consolidator/src/contract.ts holds the bar in the schema: two evidence lines are the FLOOR per candidate, because a candidate that can only cite one line is a restatement of that one line, and raw transcripts are already greppable by any agent. agent/instructions.md carries the scrutiny bar in prose."}
{"op":"add","key":"TRACE-3","patternType":"ubiquitous","systemName":"trace-consolidation phase","systemResponse":"land every synthesized memory as a reviewable commit behind the discrimination gate","priority":"critical","status":"implemented","verificationMethod":"test","verificationNote":"SHIPPED. One commit per candidate through commitPhase (packages/sleep/src/phases/trace-consolidation.ts), the same discipline every other sleep mutation takes, so every synthesized memory lands on the review branch behind the merge-time discrimination gate. The phase is absent from NON_COMMITTING_PHASES."}
{"op":"add","key":"TRACE-4","patternType":"unwanted-behavior","systemName":"trace-consolidation phase","trigger":"the model call fails or the budget of a run is exhausted","systemResponse":"leave the sleep run red or partially written","negated":true,"priority":"high","status":"implemented","verificationMethod":"test","verificationNote":"SHIPPED. INV-3 in this phase: no consolidator bound, no unconsolidated window, a dry run, or a refused call all produce `ok` with counts and a reason rather than a red run. Its state-plane watermark is deferred to the merge as a `session-consolidated` pending mark, so a discarded night leaves nothing partially written (packages/sleep/src/contract.ts, packages/sleep/src/review.ts)."}
{"op":"add","key":"TRACE-5","patternType":"event-driven","systemName":"trace-consolidation phase","trigger":"a distilled candidate frame-matches an active memory","systemResponse":"surface the conflict through the detect_conflicts assist rather than writing blind","priority":"high","status":"implemented","verificationMethod":"test","verificationNote":"SHIPPED. packages/sleep/src/phases/trace-consolidation.ts keys each candidate with frameKeyOf from @memhtml/domain and resolves a whole batch's conflicts in one lookup, attaching the live match to the candidate's commit context rather than blocking the write. A lookup failure degrades to no conflicts with a logged warning, because the assist is a note ABOUT the writes."}

