{"op":"add","key":"CODE-2","patternType":"unwanted-behavior","systemName":"memhtml exec runtime","trigger":"a sandboxed script attempts a write to the store or the index","systemResponse":"allow the mutation","negated":true,"priority":"critical","status":"implemented","verificationMethod":"test","verificationNote":"SHIPPED and mutation-verified. STORE HALF: `readOnly: true` on the OverlayFs answers EROFS and apps/cli/src/exec.ts offers no write path at all; dropping the flag makes the write succeed and fails apps/cli/tests/exec.test.ts. INDEX HALF: satisfied by REACHABILITY rather than by a guard, because read-only is no barrier to a reader (the guest's sqlite3 reads a read-only-mounted database fine, probed 2026-08-09). memhtml exec mounts a pinned commit's detached worktree and .memhtml/index.db is gitignored, so the checkout omits it."}
